WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Translator: Leslie Gauthier
Reviewer: Joanna Pietrulewicz

00:00:12.792 --> 00:00:14.393
Bruce Lee is my father,

00:00:14.417 --> 00:00:16.768
and he is best well-known
as a martial artist

00:00:16.792 --> 00:00:18.309
and an action film star,

00:00:18.333 --> 00:00:20.434
as I'm sure most of you know.

00:00:20.458 --> 00:00:22.809
He died when I was four years old,

00:00:22.833 --> 00:00:26.393
but I have a really deep memory of him.

00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:30.476
I don't have those long-form, storied
memories that you do when you're older,

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:35.792
but the memory that I do have
is of the feeling of him.

00:00:36.625 --> 00:00:38.893
I remember his energy,

00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:40.184
his presence,

00:00:40.208 --> 00:00:41.476
his love --

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:42.768
the safety of it,

00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:44.058
the power of it,

00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:45.625
the radiance of it.

00:00:46.458 --> 00:00:51.351
And to me that memory
is very deep and personal.

00:00:51.375 --> 00:00:56.792
And it is the memory of the quality
of his essential nature.

00:00:58.125 --> 00:01:00.351
What a lot of people
don't know about my father

00:01:00.375 --> 00:01:02.726
is that he was also a philosopher.

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:07.309
He had a very ever-evolving philosophy

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.851
that he lived,

00:01:09.875 --> 00:01:13.518
and it is that distinction --
that he lived his philosophy

00:01:13.542 --> 00:01:16.184
and didn't just espouse his philosophy --

00:01:16.208 --> 00:01:21.875
that made him the force of nature
that he was, and still engages us today.

00:01:22.833 --> 00:01:26.976
His wisdom has salvaged me
many times in my life:

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.934
when my brother died,

00:01:28.958 --> 00:01:30.351
when my heart's been broken,

00:01:30.375 --> 00:01:35.934
whenever I have faced a challenge
to my mind, my body or my spirit,

00:01:35.958 --> 00:01:41.583
the way that he expressed
himself has lifted me up.

00:01:42.542 --> 00:01:45.434
And so I come to you today
not as a researcher

00:01:45.458 --> 00:01:47.851
or an educator or a guru

00:01:47.875 --> 00:01:50.268
or even a life coach,

00:01:50.292 --> 00:01:52.684
but as a student of Bruce Lee --

00:01:52.708 --> 00:01:54.184
as his daughter,

00:01:54.208 --> 00:01:57.750
and also as a student of my own life.

00:01:58.625 --> 00:02:00.476
So ...

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:05.601
my big burning question that I want
you all to consider today is ...

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.000
how are you?

00:02:07.792 --> 00:02:09.042
Let me elaborate.

00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:14.559
Whenever anyone would ask my mom
what my father was like,

00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:16.976
she would say, "How he was
in front of the camera,

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.559
how you saw him in his films,

00:02:18.583 --> 00:02:20.768
how you saw him in his interviews

00:02:20.792 --> 00:02:24.268
was, in fact, exactly how he was."

00:02:24.292 --> 00:02:26.976
There were not multiple Bruce Lees.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.726
There was not public Bruce Lee
and private Bruce Lee,

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:34.059
or teacher Bruce Lee and actor Bruce Lee
and family man Bruce Lee.

00:02:34.083 --> 00:02:38.583
There was just one
unified, total Bruce Lee.

00:02:39.417 --> 00:02:44.059
And that Bruce Lee had a very deep,
philosophical life practice

00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:46.059
called self-actualization.

00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:47.941
You've probably heard that term before.

00:02:48.917 --> 00:02:53.333
It's also known as how to be yourself
in the best way possible.

00:02:54.125 --> 00:02:57.143
And that Bruce Lee said this:

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:59.309
"When I look around,
I always learn something

00:02:59.333 --> 00:03:02.476
and that is to be always yourself,

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:05.851
and to express yourself
and have faith in yourself.

00:03:05.875 --> 00:03:09.434
Don't go out and find a successful
personality and duplicate it,

00:03:09.458 --> 00:03:12.226
but rather start
from the very root of your being,

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:15.684
which is 'How can I be me?'"

00:03:15.708 --> 00:03:18.643
Many of us have done some soul-searching

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:20.934
or at least some incessant
thinking and worrying

00:03:20.958 --> 00:03:26.434
about things like our purpose,
our passion, our impact,

00:03:26.458 --> 00:03:28.125
our values

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:32.268
and our "reason for being."

00:03:32.292 --> 00:03:35.643
And that is sometimes considered our why.

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:37.893
Why am I here? Why this life?

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:40.976
What am I meant to be doing?

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:44.809
If we can grab a little piece
of that information,

00:03:44.833 --> 00:03:48.226
it can help to ground us and root us,

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.476
and it can also point us in a direction,

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:54.476
and typically what it
points us to is our what.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.976
What we manifest in the world,

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.268
what we have.

00:03:57.292 --> 00:04:02.851
So our job, our home,
our hobbies and the like.

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:06.518
But there's this little space
in between the why and the what

00:04:06.542 --> 00:04:09.601
that often doesn't get our full attention,

00:04:09.625 --> 00:04:11.601
and that is our ...

00:04:11.625 --> 00:04:12.893
how.

00:04:12.917 --> 00:04:16.167
How we get there
and the quality of that doing.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:23.518
And I want to offer that this is actually
the most important part of the equation

00:04:23.542 --> 00:04:26.143
when it comes to our personal growth,

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:28.101
our sense of wholeness

00:04:28.125 --> 00:04:32.125
and even the long-term
impact that we make.

00:04:33.958 --> 00:04:40.726
How is the action that bridges the gap
from the internal to the external.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:44.684
And bridging the gap
is a very important concept

00:04:44.708 --> 00:04:46.434
for martial artists like my father.

00:04:46.458 --> 00:04:49.226
It's how you get from point A to point B.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:54.125
It's how you get from here to your target
under the most vital of circumstances.

00:04:54.833 --> 00:04:58.101
And so it makes all the difference.

00:04:58.125 --> 00:05:00.809
Do you get there as an amateur?
Are you sloppy?

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:03.893
Are you wild, chaotic,

00:05:03.917 --> 00:05:06.726
sometimes you get lucky,
sometimes you're not lucky?

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.768
Or are you a warrior?

00:05:08.792 --> 00:05:10.726
Are you confident?

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:12.268
Are you focused?

00:05:12.292 --> 00:05:13.559
Are you skilled?

00:05:13.583 --> 00:05:14.851
Are you intuitive?

00:05:14.875 --> 00:05:17.559
Are you expressive, creative, aware?

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:22.542
So I want to talk to you today
about your how in your life.

00:05:23.333 --> 00:05:25.976
So we do a little bit of --

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.518
we spend a little time
in existential crisis

00:05:28.542 --> 00:05:31.518
over "Why am I here?
What am I meant to be doing?"

00:05:31.542 --> 00:05:35.351
and we put a ton of effort
into our what --

00:05:35.375 --> 00:05:39.684
our job, our career,
our partner that we have

00:05:39.708 --> 00:05:43.476
and the hobbies we pursue.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:45.559
But I want us to consider

00:05:45.583 --> 00:05:52.768
that our how is the expression of our why

00:05:52.792 --> 00:05:54.934
in every what,

00:05:54.958 --> 00:05:56.583
whether we're aware of it or not.

00:05:57.833 --> 00:06:00.643
And so let's take an example.

00:06:00.667 --> 00:06:04.726
Let's say that I have a value of kindness.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:06.393
I'm all about kindness,

00:06:06.417 --> 00:06:09.351
I feel really natural being kind,

00:06:09.375 --> 00:06:12.184
I want to see more kindness in the world.

00:06:12.208 --> 00:06:13.726
Is that kindness --

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:16.518
is that value in the result

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:18.125
or is it in the doing?

00:06:19.042 --> 00:06:22.667
Are you trying to be kind
when it's hard to be kind?

00:06:23.875 --> 00:06:26.684
Can you do something
you don't want to do kindly,

00:06:26.708 --> 00:06:28.684
like fire someone?

00:06:28.708 --> 00:06:31.268
Can you leave
a relationship with kindness?

00:06:31.292 --> 00:06:34.143
If kindness is the value,

00:06:34.167 --> 00:06:37.434
then are you trying to express it

00:06:37.458 --> 00:06:40.268
in the whole spectrum of your doing --

00:06:40.292 --> 00:06:43.042
and trying to do that?

00:06:44.458 --> 00:06:46.708
Or are you just doing it when it's easy?

00:06:47.208 --> 00:06:50.393
So I want us to think
about that for a moment

00:06:50.417 --> 00:06:53.476
and consider, you know, if we come home

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:58.018
and we're kind and generous
and loving with our kids,

00:06:58.042 --> 00:06:59.601
but then we go to work

00:06:59.625 --> 00:07:02.893
and we are dismissive

00:07:02.917 --> 00:07:05.809
and rude to our assistant

00:07:05.833 --> 00:07:07.768
and we treat them like a subhuman,

00:07:07.792 --> 00:07:12.833
then there is a fragmentation
in the beingness of our value.

00:07:14.083 --> 00:07:18.726
And so I want us to consider
that how we are in our lives

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:21.018
is in fact how we are.

00:07:21.042 --> 00:07:23.643
Meaning, if I am the kind of person

00:07:23.667 --> 00:07:28.018
that walks down the street
and smiles at people

00:07:28.042 --> 00:07:30.518
and says "hi" as I walk
past them on the sidewalk,

00:07:30.542 --> 00:07:32.226
then that is how I am.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:38.434
But if I'm also the kind of person
who makes fun of my brother

00:07:38.458 --> 00:07:41.809
every chance that I get behind his back,

00:07:41.833 --> 00:07:45.018
that is also the kind of person that I am.

00:07:45.042 --> 00:07:48.143
And ultimately how we are

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:51.625
makes up the totality
of the picture of who we are.

00:07:52.792 --> 00:07:57.768
And so I want to talk about
how do we unite these pieces

00:07:57.792 --> 00:07:59.268
if we have any fragmentation.

00:07:59.292 --> 00:08:03.684
I want to understand
how we embody ourselves

00:08:03.708 --> 00:08:06.851
as our one and only self.

00:08:06.875 --> 00:08:10.184
How do we actualize the whole self?

00:08:10.208 --> 00:08:13.643
My father said, "All goals
apart from the means are an illusion.

00:08:13.667 --> 00:08:16.184
There will never be means to ends --

00:08:16.208 --> 00:08:17.476
only means.

00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:20.143
And I am means.

00:08:20.167 --> 00:08:21.726
I am what I started with

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:23.059
and when it is all over,

00:08:23.083 --> 00:08:25.309
I will be all that is left."

00:08:25.333 --> 00:08:28.518
So you can employ a systematic approach
to training and practicing,

00:08:28.542 --> 00:08:31.434
but you can't employ
a systematic approach to actually living

00:08:31.458 --> 00:08:35.309
because life is a process not a goal.

00:08:35.333 --> 00:08:38.809
It is a means and not an end.

00:08:38.833 --> 00:08:41.809
So "to obtain enlightenment" --

00:08:41.833 --> 00:08:45.851
and I'm going to say self-actualize,

00:08:45.875 --> 00:08:49.351
to be self-actualized
or to obtain wholeness --

00:08:49.375 --> 00:08:51.851
"emphasis should fall
NOT on the cultivation

00:08:51.875 --> 00:08:53.433
of the particular department" --

00:08:53.457 --> 00:08:55.268
all of our whats --

00:08:55.292 --> 00:08:59.518
"which then merges into the totality
of who we are as a total human being,

00:08:59.542 --> 00:09:02.851
but rather, on the total human being

00:09:02.875 --> 00:09:08.393
that then enters into and unites
those particular departments."

00:09:08.417 --> 00:09:09.750
You are your how.

00:09:11.208 --> 00:09:12.559
You --

00:09:12.583 --> 00:09:14.851
if you have some consciousness

00:09:14.875 --> 00:09:16.643
and you want to bring some practice,

00:09:16.667 --> 00:09:19.934
if you want to step
into that warrior space

00:09:19.958 --> 00:09:21.768
around your how --

00:09:21.792 --> 00:09:26.934
how you express
in every aspect of your life --

00:09:26.958 --> 00:09:31.851
then you get to be the artist
of that expression.

00:09:31.875 --> 00:09:37.476
You get to step into that and claim it

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:39.059
and exercise it

00:09:39.083 --> 00:09:44.768
and bring that beingness
through your doingness

00:09:44.792 --> 00:09:46.625
into your havingness.

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:52.726
And there you will find
the most profound of your growth,

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:56.059
you will find a sense of wholeness

00:09:56.083 --> 00:10:00.750
and ultimately, you will leave
a lasting impact on your environment.

00:10:01.917 --> 00:10:05.143
My father was his how.

00:10:05.167 --> 00:10:10.476
He applied the execution of who he was

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:13.143
to every aspect of his life.

00:10:13.167 --> 00:10:18.042
He was way more than
that kung fu guy from the '70s.

00:10:18.833 --> 00:10:24.351
He was someone who worked very hard
at actualizing his inner self

00:10:24.375 --> 00:10:26.809
and expressing it out into the world.

00:10:26.833 --> 00:10:32.476
And that laid the foundation
for what continues to inspire us,

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:33.768
engage us,

00:10:33.792 --> 00:10:35.059
excite us

00:10:35.083 --> 00:10:37.601
and attract us to him.

00:10:37.625 --> 00:10:41.750
He was the embodied example
of living fully.

00:10:42.625 --> 00:10:47.059
He said, "I am means."

00:10:47.083 --> 00:10:48.875
And there are only means.

00:10:49.917 --> 00:10:51.750
So I'm going to ask you one more time.

00:10:53.125 --> 00:10:56.434
Thank you for listening,
and please consider,

00:10:56.458 --> 00:10:57.934
for you,

00:10:57.958 --> 00:11:01.101
across the spectrum of your doing,

00:11:01.125 --> 00:11:02.726
how are you?

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:04.018
Thank you.

00:11:04.042 --> 00:11:08.125
(Applause)

